icalWebUrl = https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/ and httpd listenUrl = proxy-https — internet-reachable push surface","docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md:293-294 'Ordinary (non-merge) story pushes for review are already allowed to Registered Users by the refs/for/refs/heads/* grant'","docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md:301-302 'Anyone may still push to refs/for/* to propose; only a Contributor/admin can Submit'"],"finding":"The plan's security justification for disabling receive.checkReferencedObjectsAreReachable rests on the premise that 'every client here is the shared bot account,' but the repo's own ACL docs show the receive/push surface (refs/for/*) is reachable by any Registered User, not only the bot — so the Gerrit-documented trust condition for safely disabling the check (clients trusted not to forge SHA-1 references to hidden commits) is not actually met as stated.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd9259b7dcd6ed8f0","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section ('every client here is the shared bot account'); AC bullet recording the trust trade-off","norm_id":"n81f59ca735b4ffd9","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A non-bot Registered User (any GitHub-OAuth account permitted to propose) pushes a thin pack whose external delta base references an object outside what their refs make reachable, exercising exactly the forged-SHA-1-reference exposure the check guards against.","The trade-off is recorded (per the last AC) as 'every client is the shared bot account,' leaving future operators with an inaccurate basis for the risk acceptance."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"medium","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["5 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an explicit back-out step (revert the gerrit.config key to default/remove it, re-run compose-up to re-seed, restart Gerrit, confirm HTTP 200) to the runbook/deploy path so the change is reversible.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.535,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'set Gerrit's receive.checkReferencedObjectsAreReachable = false server-side' changes an existing default (docs: default true)","The deploy path describes apply (compose-up + restart) but no revert procedure","T4 remedy requires an explicit rollback/back-out plan, not only acknowledgement of the trade-off"],"finding":"The plan disables a security-relevant reachability check (a behavior change with a stated trust trade-off) but states no explicit back-out/rollback step if the change fails to fix the rejections or introduces a problem.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa093ae9055786748","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Deploy path","norm_id":"nb29bdbf376e3fb15","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Note in the Deploy path that rollback is: revert the `receive.checkReferencedObjectsAreReachable` line in `infra/compose/gerrit.config`, re-run `infra/scripts/compose-up.sh`, `docker compose ... restart gerrit`, and verify the host config no longer sets `false` and the site answers HTTP 200.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the explicit rollback: revert `receive.checkReferencedObjectsAreReachable` to `true` (or remove the key) in `infra/compose/gerrit.config`, re-run compose-up to re-seed, and restart Gerrit — and note that no data cleanup is needed since the key is read only at startup.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T12"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.785,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Approach describes only the forward apply: 'compose-up.sh ... then docker compose ... restart gerrit'","Plan notes 'receive settings are read at startup, so a restart is required' — same mechanism applies to undo but is not stated as a rollback","No AC or runbook bullet states how to revert if the disabled check causes a problem"],"finding":"The plan changes runtime behavior of a deployed Gerrit (disables a receive-time check so previously-rejected pushes are now accepted) but does not state an explicit, cheap rollback path. The apply path (revert the config key in-repo, re-run compose-up to re-seed, restart Gerrit) is the obvious inverse, but it is never written down, so an operator seeing a regression has no stated undo procedure.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0140f6c3e7b17c95","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Deploy path; AC line 3","norm_id":"n04252efedb13cb81","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a rollback bullet to the Approach/runbook: the change is reversible by restoring the key to its default and restarting Gerrit; config is re-seeded from the repo so the revert is a config-only, no-data-cleanup undo.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily"